2778	Cerebria: The Inside World	Spirits of Bliss and Gloom manipulate emotions in a tug of war to represent the mind.	1	4	60	120	14	\N	https://cf.geekdo-images.com/xZ6CZ8_J4CEwR7TT8_3hKw__original/img/7Ni8b05mJH5CcKoFVbRlYrOnR1g=/0x0/filters:format(png)/pic3568532.png	\N	\N	\N	'bliss':7B 'cerebria':1A 'emot':11B 'gloom':9B 'insid':3A 'manipul':10B 'mind':20B 'repres':18B 'spirit':5B 'tug':14B 'war':16B 'world':4A	Advanced	4.34	7.74	{strategy}	2, 4	f	f	f	f		218479	Cerebria is a dynamic, team-based, objective-driven area control game, where players play as Spirits, powerful entities representing Bliss or Gloom. These opposing forces - the two sides of human nature - struggle to control and shape the Inside World, the metaphorical representation of an evolving personality.&#10; Cerebria introduces a unique theme and numerous innovative mechanisms. The game is centered around the player-controlled Spirits, and the Emotion cards controlling Cerebria&rsquo;s areas, each with their own stats and abilities.&#10;&#10;The Spirits can perform up to three actions on their turn. These include moving between Cerebria&rsquo;s Realms and Frontiers, using the specific powers of the Realms, invoking and upgrading Emotion cards, removing opposing Emotions, and building Fortresses to consolidate their influence on certain areas. The Actions cost Willpower, gained primarily by absorbing from the Origin&rsquo;s Spheres in the middle of the board. Both Bliss and Gloom also have a rare shared team resource, Ambition, enabling them to use the game&rsquo;s most powerful effects.&#10; The teams can score points either by accomplishing publicly known minor objectives (the Intentions), or completing their major objectives (the Aspirations), which change dynamically during the course of the game. Scoring Aspirations allows players to add Bliss and Gloom Fragments to the Identity, built in the middle of the board. These are key moments in the game: Cerebria&rsquo;s state is in constant flux, but the Fragments are permanent imprints of a game state during the scoring events.&#10; The game is won by the side with more influence over the finished Identity, thus becoming the dominant force in Cerebria.&#10;&#10;
2781	Cheese Factory	Choose a Chef! Build a Factory! Make the Cheese! Burn It All Down!	2	4	20	30	14	\N	https://cf.geekdo-images.com/qtTQK9kL0vgspe8in0rwug__original/img/CLsWSHzW6so91NcsRaGvkPkUlqo=/0x0/filters:format(png)/pic7259777.png	\N	\N	\N	'build':6B 'burn':12B 'chees':1A,11B 'chef':5B 'choos':3B 'factori':2A,8B 'make':9B	Lighter	0.00	7.14	{}	\N	f	f	f	f		365551	Choose a Chef, each with their own special ability: build cheese machines, collect ingredients to make the cheese and burn down your competitors factories with cheese fires!&#10;&#10;Manage your hand of ingredients and build the most effective cheese factory.&#10;&#10;The first player to make 20 points worth of cheese.&#10;&#10;
2782	Chess	Checkmate your opponent in this timeless abstract.	2	2	0	0	6	\N	https://cf.geekdo-images.com/0_RWFMNapgr5yCrdhvGi_Q__original/img/c4SiusUQuh7uc0k6HDwIXYsEc8M=/0x0/filters:format(jpeg)/pic8785991.jpg	\N	\N	\N	'abstract':8B 'checkmat':2B 'chess':1A 'oppon':4B 'timeless':7B	Classic	3.65	7.22	{}	2	t	f	f	f	4 copies	171	Chess is a two-player, abstract strategy board game that represents medieval warfare on an 8x8 board with alternating light and dark squares. Opposing pieces, traditionally designated White and Black, are initially lined up on either side of the board. Each type of piece has a unique form of movement and capturing occurs when a piece, via its movement, occupies the square of an opposing piece. Players take turns moving one of their pieces in an attempt to capture, attack, defend, or develop their positions. Chess games can end in checkmate (when the king cannot escape from the opponent's pieces), resignation (when one player recognizes that defeat is inevitable and ends the game), or one of several types of draws.&#10;&#10;Chess is one of the most popular games in the world, played by millions of people worldwide at home, in clubs, online, by correspondence, and in tournaments. Between two highly skilled players, chess can be a beautiful thing to watch, and a game can provide great entertainment even for novices. The 2020 Netflix series, The Queen's Gambit was enjoyed by both chess players and non-players alike. There is also a large literature of books and periodicals about chess, typically featuring games and commentary by chess masters. Chess is so well known and highly regarded that it is often used as a metaphor in journalism, poetry, fiction, and film.&#10;&#10;Chess has its origins in the Indian game Chaturanga, which became Shatranj when introduced to the Persians. The current form of the game emerged in the second half of the 15th century when the Persians brought Shatranj to Southern Europe. The tradition of organized competitive chess began in the 16th century. The first official World Chess Champion, Wilhelm Steinitz, claimed his title in 1886. Chess is also a recognized sport of the International Olympic Committee.&#10;&#10;
2973	Guillotine	Manipulate the line to collect the most valuable heads.	2	5	30	30	12	\N	https://cf.geekdo-images.com/9gdaUHNTcgv8RhFhG0kzBw__original/img/uJQubpcCxCE4G1pmM8akyrLAVRY=/0x0/filters:format(jpeg)/pic143139.jpg	\N	\N	\N	'collect':6B 'guillotin':1A 'head':10B 'line':4B 'manipul':2B 'valuabl':9B	Lighter	1.27	6.54	{family}	4	f	f	f	f		116	The French Revolution is famous in part for the use of the guillotine to put nobles to death, and this is the macabre subject of this light card game.  As executioners pandering to the masses, the players are trying to behead the most popular nobles.  Each day the nobles are lined up and players take turns killing the ones at the front of the line until all the nobles are gone.  However, players are given cards which will manipulate the line order right before 'harvesting' heads, which is what makes the game interesting.  After three days of chopping, the highest total carries the day.&#10;&#10;
3087	Maglev Metro	Efficiency is the key to rebuilding the city transit with maglev tech.	1	4	60	90	14	\N	https://cf.geekdo-images.com/yCj3DQLmxwdSCjXlt-styQ__original/img/hP9rjkPFC2ePsxCMwM2PqW54xHI=/0x0/filters:format(jpeg)/pic5275652.jpg	\N	\N	\N	'citi':10B 'effici':3B 'key':6B 'maglev':1A,13B 'metro':2A 'rebuild':8B 'tech':14B 'transit':11B	Advanced	2.80	7.22	{strategy}	3	f	f	f	f		301257	In Maglev Metro, utilize state-of-the-art magnetic levitation technology to build a metropolitan rail system, transporting workers and robots beneath the city. Replace aging Manhattan and Berlin subway systems with newer, faster, quieter technology. Enhance your rail system's abilities so that your passengers arrive at their destinations first.&#10;&#10;Efficiency is your key to success in this pick-up-and-deliver, tile-laying, engine-building game. Transparent tiles allow your route to overlap your opponents' tracks, winding you along from station to station. Robots efficiently upgrade and adjust your abilities, leveraging unique goals to maximize points. By the end of the game, the game board has morphed into a modern subway map, with brightly-colored routes connecting stations all over the city.&#10;&#10;Maglev Metro contains two unique maps.&#10;&#10;&mdash;description from the publisher&#10;&#10;
